# The CONTACTOS / SWITCH TEST page with contacts actually closing, which is the only
# place the firmware's own contact names render (F16).  No other capture here closes a
# matrix switch while the page is open, so all 45 names were missing from the corpus.
#
# Two things make it work.  The service menu needs no credits, so the walk is just TEST
# and eight navigation presses: F14's tree reaches record 32 (record 26's child) by
# scroll, scroll, select, select, scroll, scroll, select, select.  And inside the menu
# there is no ball in play, so the simulator's own shot keys do nothing -- Del toggles
# PinMAME's "Switch/Simulator" bit (SIM_PORTS), which hands the keyboard to the driver's
# matrix test keys instead, and those close a matrix position directly.
#
# The key-to-position map is iomoon_pf_keys in src/wpc/sleic.c: column 0 is QWERYUIO,
# column 1 ASDFGHJK, column 2 ZXCVBNML, column 3 the numeric keypad 0-7, column 4 is
# 0 2 3 4 6 8 - 9, and column 5's four fitted positions are = and keypad 8 9 -.
# Column 5's other four positions do not exist on the machine (F16).
#
# Each position is held for half a second with its own mark, so screens.csv has one
# scene per contact name.
#
# Two CABINET inputs are added at the end.  They are not matrix positions, so the matrix
# keys do not reach them, but CORE_PORTS' own cabinet keys stay live through the Del
# toggle and neither of these two navigates the menu: 5 is the coin (code 0x33 in test
# mode, F16) and T the tilt pendulum (0x3E).  The other four cabinet inputs -- START, TEST
# and the two flipper buttons -- are the menu's own navigation keys (F14), so pressing
# them here moves the menu instead of naming a contact.
    40 tap 8 KEYCODE_1
  1400 mark open-menu
  1410 tap 12 KEYCODE_7
  1600 tap 12 KEYCODE_LSHIFT
  1730 tap 12 KEYCODE_LSHIFT
  1860 tap 12 KEYCODE_RSHIFT
  1990 tap 12 KEYCODE_RSHIFT
  2120 tap 12 KEYCODE_LSHIFT
  2250 tap 12 KEYCODE_LSHIFT
  2380 tap 12 KEYCODE_RSHIFT
  2510 tap 12 KEYCODE_RSHIFT
  2640 mark svc-32-switch-test
  2840 tap 10 KEYCODE_DEL
  3040 mark contact-c0b0
  3050 tap 30 KEYCODE_Q
  3190 mark contact-c0b1
